{
  "dom_id": "step-e14309",
  "name": "Example: Multiplying Multivariable Polynomials",
  "problem": "Simplify $xy\\left(3x^2+xy+4\\right).$",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy(3{x}^{2}+xy+4) & = \\\\ (xy)\\cdot (3{x}^{2})+(xy)\\cdot (xy)+(xy)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ 3(x\\cdot {x}^{2})(y)+(x\\cdot x)(y\\cdot y)+4(xy) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{3})(y)+({x}^{2})({y}^{2})+4xy & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}y+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4xy & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
